      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Briggs%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community of Briggs developed in the post-Allotment Era within the former Cherokee Nation territory.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/briggs_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Illinois River forms the northern and western edge of the Briggs community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Briggs%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Briggs falls within the historical boundaries of the Cherokee Nation and is served by the local Briggs Public School.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/briggs_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Briggs experiences a humid subtropical climate with hot, humid summers and mild winters influenced by the Gulf of Mexico.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/briggs_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Dawes Commission facilitated the emergence of rural communities like Briggs by dividing communal Cherokee lands into individual parcels.",
